Now we need to ensure that after loading container alpha, we stage candidate alpha etc. After that, we may want to keep container alpha loaded on leg while we load beta? As discussed, seems okay.

Now we need to ensure that after we load container alpha, we do not inadvertently set origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded. Those are only set by assemble_*_loaded_leg actions, which we are not executing. So fine.

Now we need to ensure that after we load container alpha, we have transport_leg_assembled true and transport_leg_loading_authorized true (we will have done that earlier). Loading container does not affect those.

Now we need to verify loading profile nominal: requires candidate_staged_for_loading true (we will have after stage). It also requires loading_container_leg_linked true (we have). Not destination_leg_loaded true (still false). Good.

Now after verify, we set candidate_loading_verified true.

Now establish clearance nominal: requires candidate_loading_verified true, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked true, candidate_loading_container_linked true, loading_container_leg_linked true, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established. After effect, candidate_clearance_established true.

Now finalize_candidate_direct: requires candidate_clearance_established true, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized. After effect, candidate_finalized true and dispatch_ready true.

Thus we can allocate dispatch slot and execute schedule dispatch.

Now we need to ensure we have not set route_sequence_context_set anywhere else (we haven't). Good.

Now we need to also allocate dispatch slot for each candidate after they become dispatch_ready.

Now we need to ensure we have dispatch_slot_available initially true. After each allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate we set dispatch_slot unavailable; after execute_*_dispatch we set dispatch_slot_available again.

Thus we can reuse same slot.

Now we need to also ensure we have not accidentally set dispatch_ready for any candidate earlier incorrectly.

Now we need to produce the plan as a sequence of action calls.

Let's enumerate actions with parameters.

We'll use shorthand names but need to use full object names.

Define:

oa = origin_availability_alpha
da = destination_availability_alpha
sa = shift_candidate_alpha
sb = shift_candidate_beta
va = vehicle_unit_alpha
vb = vehicle_unit_beta
vg = vehicle_unit_gamma
rtp = route_task_profile_alpha
op = driver_operator_alpha
cp = cargo_payload_alpha
on = origin_node_alpha
dn = destination_node_alpha
tl = transport_leg_alpha
lcalpha = loading_container_alpha
lcbeta = loading_container_beta
eqa = equipment_resource_alpha
eqb = equipment_resource_beta
skill = skill_certificate_alpha
cc = compliance_certificate_alpha
ds = dispatch_slot_alpha

We may not need ocalpha, ocbeta, service windows.

Now step-by-step.

We'll start with origin availability.

Step 1: create_candidate oa

Step 2: allocate_vehicle_unit oa va

Step 3: attach_task_profile oa rtp

Step 4: confirm_candidate_preparedness oa rtp (note: action confirm_candidate_preparedness takes ?candidate and ?route_task_profile). So we need to pass rtp.

Step 5: assign_operator_resource oa op

Step 6: activate_origin_node oa on rtp (parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile). So activate_origin_node oa on rtp

Step 7: lock_origin_availability oa on op (parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?operator_resource - operator_resource). So lock_origin_availability oa on op

Now origin availability locked and confirmed.

Now do destination similarly.

Step 8: create_candidate da

Step 9: allocate_vehicle_unit da vb

Step 10: attach_task_profile da rtp

Step 11: confirm_candidate_preparedness da rtp

Step 12: assign_operator_resource da op

Step 13: activate_destination_node da dn rtp

Step 14: lock_destination_availability da dn op

Now origin and destination availability locked and confirmed.

Now assemble transport leg.

Step 15: assemble_transport_leg oa da on dn tl (parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?destination_node - destination_node ?transport_leg - transport_leg). So assemble_transport_leg oa da on dn tl

Now transport leg assembled, origin linked, destination linked.

Now authorize transport leg loading.

Step 16: authorize_transport_leg_loading tl oa rtp (parameters: ?transport_leg - transport_leg ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile). So authorize_transport_leg_loading tl oa rtp

Now transport leg loading authorized.

Now we can mark origin availability dispatch ready.

Step 17: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready oa tl (parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?transport_leg - transport_leg). So mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready oa tl

Now mark destination availability dispatch ready.

Step 18: mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready da tl (parameters: ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?transport_leg - transport_leg). So mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready da tl

Now we have dispatch_ready for oa and da.

Now we need to allocate dispatch slot and dispatch oa.

Step 19: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate oa ds rtp (parameters: ?candidate - candidate_entity ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile). So allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate oa ds rtp

Step 20: execute_origin_dispatch oa va ds (parameters: ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?vehicle_unit - vehicle_unit ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot). So execute_origin_dispatch oa va ds

After this, oa is dispatched, vehicle va becomes available again, dispatch slot ds becomes available.

Now we need to dispatch da similarly.

But note that after we dispatched oa, the origin_availability_alpha is dispatched; we still need it locked etc for maybe other uses? Not needed.

Now for da we need to allocate dispatch slot again (now available) and execute.

Step 21: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate da ds rtp

Step 22: execute_destination_dispatch da vb ds

Now da dispatched, vehicle vb available, slot available.

Now we need to handle schedule candidates sa and sb.

We need to prepare them similarly: create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm prepared, assign operator.

But note that we already have operator assigned to oa and da earlier; after we dispatched them, we may have released operator? We haven't released operator yet. We assigned operator to oa and da but never released. We need to release operator after we are done with lock actions (steps 6 and 14). Actually after lock we still have operator linked; we can release after lock. Let's add release_operator_resource after lock for each.

